// # scripts/ — Governance Scripts
//
// Logline: Build, test, verify, and release entry points for the
//          strategic layer (this repo).
//
// Setup: This directory is declared by RFC-0004 §5. The script
//        naming convention is `<verb>.oo` (one file, one entry
//        point). Each script takes no arguments and reads its
//        inputs from sibling files (RULES.oot, etc.).
//
// Today the auto-release logic lives in the GitHub Actions
// workflow at `.github/workflows/auto-release.yml` (not in this
// directory) — it ships zero-dep bash over gh CLI, not .oo.
// See RULES.oot §1.24 and rfcs/0006.
//
// Expected scripts (referenced by name in the RFCs, not yet
// shipped):
//
//   1. governance_enforce.oo       — verify the 256-line cap, the
//                                    ANCHOR.oo per dir rule, the
//                                    banned-name rule, and the
//                                    Academy header convention
//                                    (RFC-0003).
//   2. governance_check_boards.oo  — verify the 3-layer separation
//                                    (RFC-0004 §2): no tactical code
//                                    in the strategic repo, no
//                                    governance in tactical repos.
//   3. line_count_audit.oo         — emit the line-count report
//                                    for every tracked .oo/.oot
//                                    file.
//   4. header_compliance_smoke.oo  — assert every .oo has a 4-
//                                    element Academy header and
//                                    every .oot has the 2-line
//                                    clean header (RFC-0003).
//
// This directory follows the rule: no placeholder scripts. Each
// file is shipped only when it runs in CI and produces a non-zero
// signal on a real defect. The auto-release logic lives in
// `.github/workflows/` because the GitHub runner is the natural
// host; an .oo file would need oodac to be shipped to run.
